This extension adds Mewgenics modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Load Order and launch commands included.[/summary]

[b][color=#ffff00]Important: Vortex builds a script to launch the game based on the mods you have installed and the Load Order. You must always launch the game using the default launch tool in Vortex for the game to load mods.[/color]
[b][color=#00ff00]NOTE: Mewtator is [u]NOT[/u] required. Vortex handles load ordering and setting launch arguments.[/color][/b][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Mewtator mods with a "Mewtator.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]MewgenicsSaveEditor mods with a "MewgenicsSaveEditor.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Mewjector mods with a "version.dll" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Mods with a "description.json" file and a "data", "audio", "levels", "shaders", "swfs" or "textures" folder install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Mewjector mods with a ".dll" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Mods are installed to the "mods" folder. Load Order supported. [b]Author Note: FOMOD installers must include "mods" folder at top-level for each option.[/b][/*]
[*]Mewtator is installed to game root. Launch tool included.[/*]
[*][size=2]Includes launch tools for the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mewgenics/mods/20]Save Editor[/url]﻿ and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mewgenics/mods/190?tab=description]Level Editor[/url]﻿.[/size][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Mewgenics mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Mewtator:

Recognised when the archive contains a "Mewtator.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Saveeeditor:

Recognised when the archive contains a "MewgenicsSaveEditor.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Mewjector:

Recognised when the archive contains a "version.dll" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "description.json" file and a "data", "audio", "levels", "shaders", "swfs" or "textures" folder.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Mewjectormod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives containing a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to the built-in FOMOD installer instead.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

